    <comp lib="11" loc="(20,20)" name="Text">
      <a name="background" val="#59fffd56"/>
      <a name="format" val="wrapped"/>
      <a name="text">Poke any clock to make all clocks tick once. Or enable auto-ticks in the Simulate menu, and adjust the auto-tick frequency to your liking.
All clocks in a simulation are internally tied to a common tick source.</a>
      <a name="textwidth" val="413"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(20,260)" name="Text">
      <a name="background" val="#59fffd56"/>
      <a name="format" val="wrapped"/>
      <a name="text" val="Let's visualize different clock parameters! For this demo, it's best to enable auto-ticks and set the auto-frequecy to around 32Hz. The scopes capture and display one value per clock cycle (2 ticks), so the clocks at the left are set to use 40 or more ticks per cycle."/>
      <a name="textwidth" val="413"/>
